window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-c1cfad50412c5b58"]={"key":"ny_c-c1cfad50412c5b58","group":"ny_c","uid":"c1cfad50412c5b58","rank":94,"title":"normative audit additional premium notice 001","occupation":"customer_service_representatives","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_c3","prompt":"You are Josefa Bhandari, a customer service representative on the commercial billing desk at Orrindale Consortium. Our premium audit on Crownridge Analytics, operated by CFO Odile Pellerin, came back $46,000 short because the contractor placed crews into a second state during the policy term. We need the written audit-result notice out this week; billing lead Gustav Renko will send it to Pellerin and copy the agency. Write the customer-facing notice as `audit_additional_premium_notice.docx` and put it in the top level of the working directory where you start, using exactly that filename. Keep it to one page, with a professional letter format that can be reused by the billing desk for a comparable audit while still reading as a completed notice for this account. The letter is the act, not a discussion of how to write one, so do not give me an explanation outside the document. 1) State plainly that the audit determined additional premium of $46,000, identify the audited policy or account and audit period without making up a policy number, and distinguish the audit result from a tentative estimate. 2) Tell Odile what payment is required, when it is due, where or how payment can be arranged, and how to request the available installment option. We want to keep the account while preserving our position: the installment offer must not read as an indefinite extension, waiver, promise to renew, or agreement that the additional premium is negotiable. 3) Give the insured a practical way to question the classifications or payroll basis, including a clear contest window and the records or contact route needed to submit it, while making clear what remains payable and what happens to the collection position during review. 4) The account has operations in two states whose notice periods run differently from one due date, so select one payment date and one cancellation-related date that can be used consistently for both states and present them unambiguously; do not leave blanks, alternatives, or two competing deadlines. Make the timing defensible without quoting a statute or claiming that the letter itself changes governing law. 5) Preserve the cancellation position in firm but non-threatening language, including the consequence of nonpayment and the relationship between a timely installment arrangement, a timely dispute, and cancellation. Do not promise that submitting a dispute automatically stops cancellation. 6) Make the audience distinction work: Odile should be able to understand the amount, dates, options, and contact path without insurance jargon, while the copied agency should have enough context to help the account without being treated as the debtor. 7) Include a concise contact block addressed to the billing desk, identify Gustav Renko as the billing contact, and provide a neutral subject line and date without inventing a phone number, email address, street address, policy number, statutory citation, or other account fact. 8) A rare but serious issue has also occurred in this line of business: an audit dispute can overlap with a claim or coverage question, and a billing notice must not accidentally decide coverage, admit liability, or suggest that payment resolves a claim. Keep that exception visible in the wording or boundary of the notice, but do not turn the letter into a claims procedure. Do not include internal drafting notes, legal research, a checklist for staff, a second version, or open-ended concessions. End with the customer-facing decision and required action rather than a list of future steps.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `audit_additional_premium_notice.docx` — A one-page completed audit-result notice letter from Orrindale Consortium to Odile Pellerin at Crownridge Analytics, with the agency copied. (must be a customer-facing letter rather than an explanation or staff procedure; must fit on one page when rendered; must use exactly the supplied filename at the top level of the working directory; must not invent policy numbers, contact coordinates, statutory citations, addresses, or other account facts; must contain one coherent payment date and one coherent cancellation-related date rather than alternatives or blanks)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/audit_additional_premium_notice.docx","bytes":38385,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/0f33d029fe789cd8271363df2e90ee761a92c6da977e7ac71bfb1de2cd2dbe5b.docx","sha256":"0f33d029fe789cd8271363df2e90ee761a92c6da977e7ac71bfb1de2cd2dbe5b","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"ORRINDALE  CONSORTIUM\nCOMMERCIAL BILLING\nDate: August 25, 2026\nTo: Odile Pellerin, CFO | Crownridge Analytics\nSubject: Premium audit result and additional premium due\nDear Ms. Pellerin:\nOur completed premium audit for Crownridge Analytics' commercial policy/account, covering the audit period January 1, 2025 through January 1, 2026, determined an additional premium of $46,000.00. The audit reflects crews placed into a second state during the policy term. This is the audit result, not a tentative estimate.\nADDITIONAL PREMIUM\n$46,000.00\nPAYMENT DUE\nSeptember 24, 2026\nNONPAYMENT DATE\nOctober 19, 2026\nPayment and installment option. Please pay $46,000.00 by September 24, 2026 through your usual Orrindale billing channel, or contact Gustav Renko through the usual billing channel by September 9, 2026 to request the available installment arrangement. An installment arrangement must be confirmed in writing and remain current. It does not reduce, waive, or indefinitely extend the determined additional premium, and it does not promise renewal.\nQuestions about the audit. To request review of classifications or the payroll basis, send Gustav Renko a written explanation and the supporting payroll records, crew-location records, and classification information by September 9, 2026 through the usual billing channel. We will review a timely submission. Unless Orrindale confirms a different amount in writing, the $46,000.00 remains payable by the payment due date; review does not by itself stop billing, collection, or cancellation activity.\nNonpayment. If the amount is not paid by September 24, 2026 and no timely installment arrangement has been confirmed and kept current, Orrindale may pursue collection and may cancel for nonpayment effective October 19, 2026, subject to the policy terms and applicable requirements. A timely audit question does not automatically prevent cancellation. This single timetable is being used consistently for the operations reviewed in both states; it does not change governing policy or legal requirements.\nThis billing notice addresses premium only. It does not determine coverage, liability, or the resolution of any claim, and payment of this additional premium does not resolve a separate claim or coverage question.\nBilling contact: Gustav Renko, Commercial Billing Desk | Please use your usual Orrindale billing channel.\nPlease arrange payment or a written installment arrangement by the dates above; otherwise, the additional premium is due September 24, 2026 and the account may be cancelled for nonpayment effective October 19, 2026.\nSincerely,\nOrrindale Consortium\nCommercial Billing Desk\ncc: Agency of Record (for assistance to Crownridge Analytics)","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted deliverable is a readable DOCX file named `audit_additional_premium_notice.docx`.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filename and successful document opening.","grader_hint":"Inspect the working-directory filename and open the DOCX."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered customer-facing notice occupies no more than one page.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX with a standard office renderer and count pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice identifies Orrindale Consortium as sender and Crownridge Analytics as the audited customer, with Odile Pellerin identified as recipient or CFO.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Letterhead, address block, salutation, or body text.","grader_hint":"Search the rendered text for all three required names."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice states that the audit determined additional premium of $46,000 and presents it as an assessed or determined amount, not a proposal or estimate.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Amount and decisive audit-result wording in the body.","grader_hint":"Confirm both the exact amount and non-tentative characterization."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice identifies the relevant policy or account and audit period without fabricating a policy number or unsupported account identifier.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reference line and audit description.","grader_hint":"Credit if the scope is understandable and no invented identifier is presented as fact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice states the payment amount and a single unambiguous payment due date.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Payment paragraph or amount-due block.","grader_hint":"There must be one operative date, not a blank, range, or competing alternative."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice explains how to request the installment option and makes the option operationally actionable.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Installment paragraph and contact instructions.","grader_hint":"Look for a clear request route and a condition or deadline for arranging installments."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The installment language offers flexibility without waiving, reducing, indefinitely extending, or making negotiable the determined additional premium.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Combined reading of amount, installment, and reservation language.","grader_hint":"Credit only when the option is bounded and the $46,000 obligation remains clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice provides a clear method and deadline for questioning audit classifications or the payroll basis.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dispute or review paragraph.","grader_hint":"A reader must know what to submit, to whom, and by when."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice distinguishes a timely audit dispute from payment obligations and does not state that merely disputing the audit automatically suspends collection or cancellation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Interaction of dispute and payment/cancellation paragraphs.","grader_hint":"Look for preserved collection rights and a qualification that review does not itself create an automatic stay."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice states one coherent cancellation-related date tied to nonpayment.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cancellation or nonpayment paragraph.","grader_hint":"The date must be explicit and singular."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The payment due date and cancellation-related date are chronologically coherent, with cancellation occurring after the payment deadline and with sufficient notice for the more protective of the two applicable state timing requirements.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dates and their stated relationship in the notice.","grader_hint":"Check date ordering and whether the notice adopts one conservative timetable rather than separate conflicting state deadlines."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice preserves Orrindale Consortium's cancellation and collection position while avoiding an unsupported claim that the letter overrides governing policy or state law.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reservation, nonpayment, and governing-terms language.","grader_hint":"The letter should be firm, qualified where necessary, and not purport to rewrite legal requirements."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The agency is identified as copied or receiving a copy, without being described as the party responsible for the additional premium.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"cc line or equivalent audience designation.","grader_hint":"Credit for a clear agency-copy treatment and no misidentification of debtor."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A CFO can understand the amount, deadline, installment choice, dispute route, and consequence of inaction without needing the author to explain insurance terminology.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole-document usability and plain-language review.","grader_hint":"Judge whether the letter is actionable for Odile on first reading."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice identifies Gustav Renko as the billing contact and gives a usable contact instruction without inventing contact coordinates.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Closing or contact block.","grader_hint":"A neutral instruction such as contacting Gustav Renko through the usual billing channel is acceptable; fabricated phone numbers or email addresses are not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The notice states or clearly implies that the billing audit result does not determine claim coverage, liability, or resolution of a separate claim.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Boundary or reservation language in the letter.","grader_hint":"The exception must be visible without becoming a claims-handling procedure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document contains no invented policy number, street address, phone number, email address, statutory citation, or other unsupported account fact.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fact audit against the request.","grader_hint":"Treat placeholders or clearly labeled fields differently from fabricated completed facts; this is a credit item for disciplined sourcing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The letter ends with a clear customer-facing determination and required action, rather than an internal checklist, open-ended negotiation, or list of future steps.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final paragraph and closing.","grader_hint":"The ending should leave the recipient knowing what to do and by when."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document does not include a second version of the letter, internal drafting notes, legal research, or a staff checklist.","weight":-4.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole-document inspection.","grader_hint":"Apply the penalty only for over-production of these excluded materials; do not separately penalize ordinary explanatory sentences needed in the customer letter."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a customer-facing insurance billing communication prepared by a finance and insurance customer service representative for an audited commercial account. The document must be operationally usable by the billing desk, understandable to the insured CFO, and suitable for copying to the agency.","difficulty_sources":["balancing collection, cancellation, and customer-complaint risks in a single customer-facing notice","selecting one coherent payment and cancellation timetable that works across two state requirements","translating a premium-audit outcome into a reusable, audience-appropriate letter without inventing unsupported policy facts","handling a rare severe coverage-sensitive exception without allowing it to distort the ordinary notice"],"authoring_plan":{"purpose":"Construct a one-page customer-facing audit-result notice that makes the $46,000 additional premium a final audit determination, gives a bounded installment path, preserves collection and cancellation rights, and remains understandable and non-accusatory.","source_facts":{"carrier":"Orrindale Consortium","insured":"Crownridge Analytics","recipient":"Odile Pellerin, CFO","billing_contact":"Gustav Renko","audit_reason":"Crews were placed into a second state during the policy term.","additional_premium":46000,"agency_copy":true},"required_professional_content":["A dated letter with a neutral subject and clear sender, recipient, and copy treatment.","A plain statement that the audit determined $46,000 in additional premium, with policy/account and audit-period scope described without invented identifiers.","A single payment deadline and a single later cancellation-related date, selected conservatively enough to accommodate the more protective applicable notice timing.","A bounded installment option requiring affirmative arrangement rather than open-ended flexibility.","A classification/payroll review route with a definite contest window and practical submission instructions.","Language preserving payment, collection, and cancellation rights while avoiding an automatic-stay promise for a dispute.","A concise non-coverage boundary so the billing letter does not decide a claim, coverage, or liability issue.","A usable closing naming Gustav Renko and a generic, non-fabricated billing contact route."],"tension_design":{"collision":"The notice must be firm enough to preserve cancellation and collection rights while offering an installment option and a contest route that are fair and usable. The gold should resolve this with one bounded option, one deadline structure, and explicit non-waiver language rather than with threats or indefinite discretion.","rare_severe_exception":"Include a narrow boundary for the possibility that an audit dispute overlaps a claim or coverage question. The notice must not decide coverage, admit liability, or imply that paying the audit resolves a claim."},"gold_derivation":"Draft a completed notice using internally consistent synthetic dates. Make the payment deadline precede the cancellation-related date by a defensible margin and use the same dates throughout. Avoid statutory citations and unsupported account details. Render the DOCX to verify one-page geometry, then inspect the text against every rubric item, including the single over-production penalty."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"audit_additional_premium_notice","filename":"audit_additional_premium_notice.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A one-page completed audit-result notice letter from Orrindale Consortium to Odile Pellerin at Crownridge Analytics, with the agency copied.","required":true,"constraints":["must be a customer-facing letter rather than an explanation or staff procedure","must fit on one page when rendered","must use exactly the supplied filename at the top level of the working directory","must not invent policy numbers, contact coordinates, statutory citations, addresses, or other account facts","must contain one coherent payment date and one coherent cancellation-related date rather than alternatives or blanks"],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"form_or_template","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"customer_service_representatives","sector":"finance_insurance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":2.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have one insurance-billing practitioner review customer usability, audit-notice completeness, and cancellation/dispute wording, and have an independent document reviewer verify dates, unsupported facts, page count, and rubric reachability.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No supplied policy form or state-law reference is available, so the gold should be judged on internally coherent conservative timing and avoidance of unsupported statutory claims rather than on a hidden jurisdiction-specific day count.","The final notice may use a clearly identified generic billing contact route because no real contact coordinates are supplied."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:46:18+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:46:18+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:46:18+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:46:18+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R04']","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:46:18+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c3/runs/c1cfad50412c5b58","declared_deliverables":["audit_additional_premium_notice.docx"]};
